 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A six-child pediatric Evans syndrome cohort in which one identifiable child (Table 1 patient 3) carries a TNFAIP3 VUS: 'a heterozygous missense variant in the TNFAIP3 gene (c.1733C>T; p.Ser578Phe) was identified'; her carrier mother and non-carrier father are also described.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; no table was transcribed by script (a short script only assembled the JSON and checked spans). Scope: of 6 cohort patients (cohort_size_as_stated = 6), only one has a TNFAIP3 variant; the other 5 get no rows. The text says 'In one child' without a label; Table 1 (patients as rows, column 'Patient') shows 'TNFAIP3 VUS' only in row 3, so that child is labelled 'Patient 3' (rule 1; the paper prints only '3' under the 'Patient' header and never writes 'Patient 3'). Relatives: the mother (carrier, clinically asymptomatic) and the father (variant absent) are described in relation to Patient 3 and get rows; the father has no variant row because the variant was absent in him. Mother's zygosity and her own inheritance are not stated, so recorded as not reported; her variant row reuses the only printed variant string, tied to her by the trio statement. Age at onset = Table 1 'Age at First Cytopenia' (3); units are years per the text ('range 3–15 years') and Table 2; note one unnamed patient had an IM before first cytopenia, so symptom onset may differ if that was Patient 3. AIN column 'No' for Patient 3 was treated as an explicit word answer (not a symbol) and recorded as excluded. Sacroiliitis was mapped to checklist 'arthritis or arthralgia' as observed. AIHA was not recorded for Patient 3: the paper does not state it individually, and two cohort patients met ES criteria without overt hemolysis. 'All patients experienced relapsing disease' and 'All six patients received first-line therapy' were applied to Patient 3 as group statements naming the whole cohort. The mother's 'no history of autoimmune or autoinflammatory disease' was recorded as one excluded phenotypic_features row and not mapped to specific checklist items (left not reported). Ethnicity/country left not reported: the paper gives the referral center's catchment area in Greece, not the patients' origin. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients left null: the paper does not mention any earlier description of these patients. No contradictions found in the paper.",
